Declaration:
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_Task
VAR_INPUT
  PartPulse : BOOL;
  Reset : BOOL;
  Target : USINT;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
  Count : USINT;
  Complete : BOOL;
  Error : BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR
  qPulse : BOOL := FALSE;
  qCount : USINT := 0;
END_VAR

Implementation:
Error := (Target < 1) OR (Target > 20);
IF Error OR Reset THEN
  Count := 0;
  Complete := FALSE;
ELSE
  IF PartPulse AND NOT qPulse THEN
    IF Count < Target THEN
      Count := Count + 1;
    END_IF;
  END_IF;
  IF Count >= Target THEN
    Complete := TRUE;
  ELSE
    Complete := FALSE;
  END_IF;
END_IF;
qPulse := PartPulse;

Wait P5: G(PartPulse -> X qPulse) — qPulse after scan updated to PartPulse, yes.

Initialization: Count output on first scan. If Target invalid or reset, clears. Otherwise, count starts at 0 (retained Count defaults 0). But first scan normally, Count is 0 initially — edge if pulse high at first scan: qPulse FALSE initially so rise, Count=1. Consistent with "Step 0 executes normally; initial conditions describe pre-state." Good.

Note "Complete remains TRUE until reset or invalid; a higher Target can clear it." My code: if Count >= Target Complete TRUE else FALSE, so higher target clears. Good.

USINT comparison to 1 fine. Target > 20 fine.

Careful: Count output variable used as retained state; it's an output, retained. Fine.

Let's compile.

